{
  "schema_version": "offline-clone.routes.v1",
  "routes": [
    {
      "id": "home",
      "route_pattern": "/",
      "priority": "p0",
      "purpose_edge": "primary",
      "evidence_kind": "directly-observed",
      "local_destination": true,
      "roles": [
        "visitor"
      ],
      "states": [
        "loaded",
        "nav-product",
        "nav-apps",
        "nav-resources",
        "mobile-menu"
      ],
      "note": "WordPress + Astra marketing entry. Rendered top-level nav is Product, Apps, Resources, Help, Pricing plus My Account and Get Started; 'Features' and 'Solutions' appear in served markup but never render. Ships a WPML 'registered on wpml.org as a development site' banner in production."
    },
    {
      "id": "pricing",
      "route_pattern": "/pricing/",
      "priority": "p0",
      "purpose_edge": "primary",
      "evidence_kind": "directly-observed",
      "local_destination": true,
      "roles": [
        "visitor"
      ],
      "states": [
        "2-year",
        "yearly",
        "monthly"
      ],
      "note": "The P0 comparison surface. Three billing-period tabs rendered as bare <strong> elements (2-Year Plan default / Yearly Plan / Monthly Plan), each with Essential and Advanced tiers; Advanced carries a 'Best Protection' ribbon. Monthly $14.99/$17.99; Yearly $3.89/$5.39 per month struck from $179.88/$215.88 with '$46.68/$64.68 for the first year'; 2-Year $2.49/$3.59 struck from $359.76/$431.76. 'View All Features \u2228' / 'Hide All Features \u2227' expanders exist in the mobile plan panels and render at viewports <=767px; an earlier desktop-only probe wrongly concluded they never render, and that claim is corrected here. The checkout quote is priced by a non-GET request, so a GET-only capture of the chooser shows $0.00 line items; the resolved figures ($179.88 struck, Save 74% -$133.20, Estimated tax $6.07, Total due $52.75 for essential-annual) come from an interactive probe and are corroborated by catalogue arithmetic."
    },
    {
      "id": "checkout-chooser",
      "route_pattern": "/checkout/address-payment-method",
      "priority": "p0",
      "purpose_edge": "primary",
      "evidence_kind": "directly-observed",
      "local_destination": true,
      "roles": [
        "visitor"
      ],
      "states": [
        "essential-annual",
        "essential-monthly",
        "advanced-annual",
        "card-form",
        "sandbox-approved",
        "sandbox-declined",
        "sandbox-retry"
      ],
      "note": "On the source this is an Angular SPA on the linked subdomain checkout.ipvanish.com, entered as ?flow={tier}-{period}&currency=USD&lang=EN. Step one is a payment-method chooser (Credit card / PayPal / Apple Pay / Google Pay) beside an Order Summary; for essential-annual: 12 months, IPVanish Essential $179.88, Save 74% - $133.20, Estimated tax $6.07, Total due $52.75. Activating the Credit card row expands the registration form. The clone serves this on its own origin under the same path; the sandbox-* states are clone-local payment behaviour."
    },
    {
      "id": "sso-signin",
      "route_pattern": "/login",
      "priority": "p0",
      "purpose_edge": "primary",
      "evidence_kind": "directly-observed",
      "local_destination": true,
      "roles": [
        "visitor"
      ],
      "states": [
        "loaded",
        "validation-error"
      ],
      "note": "Source serves this from sso.ipvanish.com (Next.js SPA); www.ipvanish.com/login/ 301s there. Copy: 'RECLAIM YOUR ONLINE PRIVACY TODAY', 'Not a member? Sign up now!' linking to /pricing/, 'Welcome back! Sign in to continue to customer portal', Email address, Password, 'Forgot password?'. Inputs named email and password. No third-party identity-provider buttons were observed."
    },
    {
      "id": "sso-recovery",
      "route_pattern": "/login/reset-password",
      "priority": "p1",
      "purpose_edge": "supporting",
      "evidence_kind": "directly-observed",
      "local_destination": true,
      "roles": [
        "visitor"
      ],
      "states": [
        "loaded",
        "validation-error",
        "sent"
      ],
      "note": "Reachable only by clicking 'Forgot password?'; the source's un-slashed /reset-password deep link answers 403 from its S3 origin while /reset-password/ works. Copy: 'Reset password', 'Enter you account email, you will receive a reset password code' (source typo, reproduced verbatim), Email address, 'Back to sign in', 'Send code'. Input named username."
    },
